<title>FINLAND: Finnish prelim March trade surplus FIM 3.0 bln - NCB.</title>
<headline>Finnish prelim March trade surplus FIM 3.0 bln - NCB.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finland's trade surplus rose to 3.5 billion markka in March from 3.0 billion in February and from 2.97 billion in March last year, the National Customs Board (NCB) said in statement on Monday.</p>
<p>It said the figures were preliminary.</p>
<p>The value of exports rose six percent year-on-year in March and the value of imports rose three percent, NCB said.  </p>
<p>Trade balance (million markka):</p>
<p>		  Mar '97    Feb '97    Mar '96</p>
<p> Exports	 16,000     14,437     15,075</p>
<p> Imports	 12,500     11,430     12,105</p>
<p> Balance	 +3,500     +3,007     +2,970</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
